  displayName: Powhatan
  leader: Wahunsenacawh
  date: c. 1607
  biography: Wahunsenacawh was the paramount chief known to the English as Powhatan. He led a chiefdom of multiple communities when Jamestown was founded in 1607.
  region: Tidewater Virginia and the Chesapeake coastal plain.
  terrain:
  - Broadleaf Forest
  - Prairie
  - Swamp
  goods:
  - Food
  - Tobacco
  jobs:
  - Farmers
  - Tobacco Planters
  rival: Monacan
  scenarioAggression: Medium
  contextNote: Monacan is a documented regional rival. Food reflects maize agriculture; Tobacco is a simplified game category for Indigenous tobacco, not a European plantation uniform.
  sources:
  - https://www.nps.gov/people/powhatan.htm
  - https://www.nps.gov/cajo/planyourvisit/werowocomoco.htm
  - https://www.nps.gov/prwi/learn/historyculture/americanindian.htm
